  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We proceed as follows:\n\n- First, we split each whole into sixths.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/0f1ad639c2ea37dd2cd777ef01f7fe51acd1a90c1afa6782698a188f61c63381.png)\n\n \n\n- Next, we create groups of $\\frac{2}{6}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/17806a28d4b4dd3f604030460809a43a1282c3f06b412fa4a3a2f4fcb43e47d2.png)\n\n \n\n- Then, we count the groups.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144297/assets/cc0f841b8652f3589b381c9f434afccaab62bf8ea691ee6fdd0edd4776f24694.png)\n\n \n\nSo, if we divide $2$ wholes into groups of $\\frac{2}{6},$ we get $6$ groups in total.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n2÷\\frac{2}{6}=6.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
